# Application Service Rules

You are writing an application service in the **Application Layer**.
This layer orchestrates use cases. It coordinates between domain and infrastructure.

## Your responsibilities
- Implement use cases (one public method per use case)
- Call domain entities' business methods
- Call repository interfaces (via injected interfaces, NOT concrete types)
- Emit events for async side effects (email, notifications)
- Handle transaction boundaries (via UnitOfWork interface for multi-table writes)
- Convert domain entities to DTOs for the return value

## What you MUST NOT do
- Import `net/http`, `github.com/gin-gonic/gin`, or any HTTP framework
- Import infrastructure packages directly (no `infrastructure/persistence/...`)
- Import `gorm.io/gorm` — this project does not use GORM
- Throw HTTP status codes or HTTP exceptions
- Call another module's repository directly

## Interface definition (always create the interface first)
```go
// i_[name]_service.go
package service

import (
    "context"
    "[module]/internal/[domain]/controller/dto"
)

type I[Name]Service interface {
    Create(ctx context.Context, req *dto.Create[Name]Req) (*dto.[Name]Resp, error)
    FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*dto.[Name]Resp, error)
    List(ctx context.Context, filter *dto.List[Name]Filter) (*dto.PaginatedResp[[Name]Resp], error)
    Update(ctx context.Context, id string, req *dto.Update[Name]Req) (*dto.[Name]Resp, error)
    Delete(ctx context.Context, id string) error
}
```

## Implementation pattern
```go
// [name]_service.go
package service

import (
    "context"
    "fmt"
    "time"

    "[module]/internal/[domain]/domain"
    domainEntity "[module]/internal/[domain]/domain/model/entity"
    domainRepo "[module]/internal/[domain]/domain/repository"
    "[module]/internal/[domain]/controller/dto"
)

type [Name]Service struct {
    repo      domainRepo.I[Name]Repository  // INTERFACE, not concrete type
    eventBus  event.IBus                    // INTERFACE
    // other dependencies — all interfaces
}

func New[Name]Service(repo domainRepo.I[Name]Repository, bus event.IBus) I[Name]Service {
    return &[Name]Service{repo: repo, eventBus: bus}
}

func (s *[Name]Service) Create(ctx context.Context, req *dto.Create[Name]Req) (*dto.[Name]Resp, error) {
    // 1. Business validation (if not in entity constructor)
    if req.Amount <= 0 {
        return nil, domain.ErrInvalidAmount
    }

    // 2. Create domain entity
    e := &domainEntity.[Name]{
        ID:        uuid.New().String(),
        // ... map from req
        CreatedAt: time.Now(),
    }

    // 3. Persist
    if err := s.repo.Save(ctx, e); err != nil {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("[name]Service.Create: %w", err)
    }

    // 4. Side effects (non-blocking)
    s.eventBus.Emit("[name].created", &event.[Name]CreatedEvent{ID: e.ID})

    // 5. Return DTO (not entity)
    return toResp(e), nil
}

// toResp is private — converts entity to DTO
func toResp(e *domainEntity.[Name]) *dto.[Name]Resp {
    return &dto.[Name]Resp{
        ID: e.ID,
        // map fields
    }
}
```

## Error handling in service
```go
// Wrap errors with operation context
return nil, fmt.Errorf("[name]Service.FindByID id=%s: %w", id, err)

// Domain errors: just return them directly (they're already descriptive)
if !entity.IsValid() {
    return nil, domain.ErrInvalidState
}

// Never: return http.StatusBadRequest, nil — wrong layer
```
